    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Inspect metadata for a known material resource ID.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h, --help                            Print this help message and exit\r\n      --resource-id TEXT REQUIRED       Material resource ID returned by `material search`, `material\r\n                                        topic`, or another trusted material result.\r\n      --type <music|sticker|effect|transition|text_template|audio|...> \r\n                                        Optional material asset type key. Use `music` to force Music\r\n                                        query; other types enable Loki fallback with source=2 when Artist\r\n                                        query is empty.\r\n      --channel <online|test|local_test> \r\n                                        Material request channel. Use `test` or `local_test` for internal\r\n                                        test resources.\r\n  -v, --version                         Show version information and exit.\r\n      --jq TEXT                         Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                                        .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                                        the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nWHEN TO USE\r\n  - You already have a resource_id and need title, cover, source, download URLs, or music metadata.\r\n  - You need to confirm a material before download or draft handoff.\r\n\r\nROUTING\r\n  By default, query checks the visual/audio material library first, then music.\r\n  Use `--type <type>` to allow Loki fallback with the matching material effect_type.\r\n  Use `--type music` when the resource ID is known to be music.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli material query --resource-id \"7586591573920664856\"\r\n  $ lyra-cli material query --resource-id \"7133105682881974821\" --type effect\r\n  $ lyra-cli material query --resource-id \"6702218125842057217\" --type music\r\n\r\nOUTPUT\r\n  Returns normalized metadata in result.items[].\r\n",
